id: pm-jiusod
title: "Four edge-counting conventions publish under one edge_count field: graph analyze reports 10046 and graph centrality 7351 for the same graph at the same cache fingerprint"
description: "pm graph subcommands emit directed, undirected, deduplicated, and fixture edge counts under one undeclared field name, so cross-subcommand comparison reports phantom edge loss."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: contracts,data-quality,graph,observability,pm-cli
created_at: "2026-07-31T06:02:33.984Z"
updated_at: "2026-07-31T08:31:58.331Z"
closed_at: "2026-07-31T08:31:13.427Z"
completed_at: "2026-07-31T08:31:13.427Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: "Every graph subcommand emitting edge_count also emits the basis that produced it; A contract test asserts basis presence and cross-subcommand agreement within a basis for one cache fingerprint; The unconditional degreeSum/2 halving is either justified by an asserted undirected adjacency or made conditional on the directed flag already in scope; graph audit profile totals reconcile against a directly derived stored-edge count, or the canonicalization it applies is declared"
value: Makes graph size a trustworthy measurement so enrichment waves can be verified rather than believed.
why_now: The tracker is entering a deliberate graph enrichment programme; edge_count is the before/after measure and it currently has four meanings.
parent: pm-96h7
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: "Added explicit edge_count_basis values for directed-deduplicated, simple-undirected, and fixture-generated conventions across all emitting surfaces."
expected_result: "Every pm graph subcommand that emits edge_count declares the counting convention it used, and two subcommands sharing a convention agree for one fingerprint."
actual_result: "analyze emits 10046 (directed stored edges), centrality emits 7351 (degreeSum/2, undirected), audit profile emits 10046 against 10499 raw stored edges; no envelope names its basis."
component: sdk/graph
