close_reason: "Delivered explicit edge-count basis contracts across SDK graph surfaces, documentation, focused tests, packed acceptance, and full release-gate proof."
body: "## Measured 2026-07-31 at HEAD\n\nTwo subcommands of `pm graph`, run back to back against the same workspace and reporting the same cache fingerprint `d9ffaeb9eaa5`, disagree about how large the graph is:\n\n- `pm graph analyze --json` -> `edge_count: 10046`\n- `pm graph centrality --json` -> `edge_count: 7351`\n\nSame field name, same command, same node_count of 2222, same fingerprint, 26.8 percent apart. Nothing in either envelope names the convention it used.\n\n## Root cause\n\n`src/sdk/graph/run.ts:834` emits `graph.edges().length` — the directed count of stored edges.\n`src/sdk/graph/centrality.ts:273` emits `edgeCount: degreeSum / 2` — an undirected count derived by halving the adjacency degree sum.\n\nBoth values are individually correct for their own analytic. Neither is labelled. A `directed` flag is already in scope at the centrality call site and is passed to `centralityRow`, but the halving is applied unconditionally, so on a genuinely directed adjacency the reported value is not a count of anything.\n\n## Why this matters beyond cosmetics\n\n`edge_count` is the field an agent uses to decide whether a traversal is affordable and whether a graph enrichment wave changed anything. Two conventions under one name make every cross-subcommand comparison wrong in a way that reads as data loss: an agent that reads centrality after analyze concludes 2,695 edges disappeared. It is also the exact shape of defect the cross-channel-disagreement catalog entry on the relevance engine describes — two channels that should agree about one fact, with no predicate stating which is authoritative.\n\n## The general form\n\nThe graph command family has at least three independent edge-counting sites: the two above plus `src/sdk/graph/conformance.ts:74` (fixture-declared) and `src/sdk/dependencies.ts:653` (deduplicated by `source::target::kind` key). The audit profile reports 10046 while a direct read of the stored `dependencies[]` arrays plus parent-field edges totals 10499, so a fourth canonicalization is applied somewhere in the audit path. Four counting conventions, one field name, zero declarations.\n\n## Minimal correct shape\n\n`edge_count` declares its convention in the envelope (`edge_basis: directed | undirected | deduplicated`), or the field is renamed per convention so no two subcommands publish different semantics under one key. Whichever is chosen, a contract test asserts that every subcommand of `pm graph` that emits `edge_count` also emits its basis, and that two subcommands sharing a basis report the same number for the same fingerprint."
